ed classes and add unit tests\n\n* feat: move criterion to vo\n\n* feat: add null checks for constructors in Choice, Criterion, and CriterionText; improve error handling in accessors\n\n* feat: Introduce immutable value objects and interfaces for form management\n\n* feat: Implement immutable value objects and interfaces for run management, enhancing data integrity and encapsulation\n\n* feat: Add unit tests for value objects in Runs domain, ensuring invariants and accessors are validated\n\n* feat: Refactor value objects and interfaces to use abstractions, enhancing type safety and flexibility\n\n* feat: Implement interfaces for EvaluationForm and FormRun aggregates, enhancing abstraction and testability\n\n* feat: Refactor value objects to remove nullable types and introduce null object patterns for improved safety and clarity\n\n* feat: Add validation to value objects for non-empty codes and names, and enforce period constraints\n\n* feat: iid\n\n* feat: Refactor interfaces and value objects to use abstractions for improved type safety and clarity\n\n* feat: Refactor evaluation form handling by introducing RunFormSnapshot, RunFormGroup, and RunFormCriterion for improved structure and clarity\n\n* feat: Introduce calculation policies for form snapshots with arithmetic and weighted mean implementations\n\n* feat: Refactor evaluation form and run form structures by removing weight properties and introducing calculation policy snapshots\n\n* refactor: remove FormCalculationKind enum and related logic\n\n- Deleted the FormCalculationKind enum as it was no longer needed.\n- Updated EvaluationForm to remove references to FormCalculationKind.\n- Refactored Snapshot methods to use calculation policies directly instead of relying on the enum.\n- Modified RunFormSnapshot to accept a calculation policy instead of a calculation rule.\n- Adjusted related classes and tests to accommodate the removal of the enum and ensure proper functionality with the new policy-based approach.\n\n* feat: Refactor EvaluationForm to use calculation policy definition and remove weighted definitions\n\n* feat: Add unit tests for ArithmeticMeanPolicy and WeightedMeanPolicy definitions and calculations\n\n* feat: Refactor evaluation form and related value objects\n\n- Changed the identifier type in EvaluationForm from Uuid to IId.\n- Removed unnecessary using directives across various files.\n- Updated references to IChoice and other interfaces to use the simplified namespace.\n- Cleaned up the WeightedMeanPolicy class by removing unused usings and simplifying logic.\n- Refactored tests to align with the new structure and interfaces.\n- Removed redundant methods and comments in interfaces and value objects.\n- Ensured consistency in naming and usage of value objects across the domain.\n\n* feat: Introduce strongly-typed identifiers for evaluation forms, runs, agreements, and related entities; refactor existing code to utilize new identifiers and remove obsolete components\n\n* refactor: Simplify identifier usage in EvaluationForm and FormRun constructors\n\n* feat: Add agreements and forms interfaces and enums for run agreements and evaluation forms\n\n* Refactor agreement and form interfaces and entities\n\n- Updated namespaces for RunAgreementStatus, RunAgreementDecision, and RunAgreementView to reflect their association with Agreements.\n- Modified imports in various files to use the new Agreements namespace.\n- Added missing interfaces for forms in several value objects and policies.\n- Adjusted tests to accommodate the new structure and ensure proper references to the updated namespaces and interfaces.\n\n* feat: Refactor evaluation form and run-related entities to use strongly-typed identifiers and remove obsolete components\n\n* feat: Introduce NoAssessment class and refactor assessment handling in policies and scores to improve null safety\n\n* refactor: Remove unused interface imports across various entities and tests to streamline code\n\n* refactor: Replace IId with strongly-typed identifiers across agreements, forms, and policies for improved type safety\n\n* refactor: Update namespaces and reorganize value objects in the Runs and Forms domains\n\n- Changed namespaces for RunContext, RunCriterionScore, RunLifecycle, RunMeta, RunResult, and RunState to align with the new structure.\n- Introduced new value objects for Forms including AuditTrail, BpsOfPercent, Choice, Criterion, CriterionText, FormCode, FormCriterion, FormGroup, FormLifecycle, FormMeta, FormName, NoPeriod, OrderIndex, Period, Weight.\n- Implemented null object patterns for NoAssessment and NoPeriod.\n- Enhanced Run lifecycle management with detailed timestamps and context handling.\n- Improved validation and error handling across various value objects.\n\n* refactor: Remove BpsOfPercent value object and its associated tests to streamline codebase\n\n* refactor: Replace IPeriod interface with Period value object for improved type safety and clarity in form lifecycle management\n\n* refactor: Replace IOrderIndex interface with OrderIndex value object for improved type safety and clarity in form management\n\n* refactor: Remove ToString method from FormCode and FormName value objects for cleaner code\nrefactor: Remove unused using directive in FormLifecycle value object\nrefactor: Remove unused using directive in OrderIndexTests\n\n* refactor: Replace interface-based value objects with concrete implementations for improved clarity and type safety in forms\n\n* refactor: Replace interface-based lifecycle and audit trail with concrete value objects for improved clarity and type safety\n\n* feat: Add Option value object to model presence or absence without using null\n\n* test: Add unit tests for Option value object covering mapping, binding, and reduction\n\n* feat: Implement form lifecycle management with audit tail for EvaluationForm\n\n* refactor: Simplify FormLifecycle and EvaluationForm by removing status parameter and adding Status method\n\n* feat: Add domain events for form lifecycle management including FormArchived, FormCreated, FormEdited, and FormPublished\nfeat: Implement immutable form audit entry with changes tracking\nfeat: Introduce FormChange value object for field-level change representation\n\n* feat: Refactor form audit entries and changes to improve audit management\n\n* feat: Enhance EvaluationFormConfiguration with detailed meta property mappings and value comparers\n\n* feat: Update FormAuditTail and EvaluationFormConfiguration to remove Stamp property and enhance lifecycle management\n\n* feat: Replace IFormGroup and IFormCriterion with FormGroup and FormCriterion for consistency across the evaluation form domain\n\n* feat: Refactor WeightedMeanPolicy and related classes to simplify property access and improve consistency\n\n* feat: Refactor WeightedMeanPolicy to streamline score and weight calculations, enhancing readability and maintainability\n\n* feat: Refactor evaluation domain interfaces and value objects to remove unused interfaces and improve type consistency\n\n* feat: Remove unused IFormRun and IWeight interfaces to streamline the evaluation domain\n\n* feat: Add JSON serialization and deserialization for FormGroup and FormCriterion collections in EvaluationFormConfiguration\n\n* feat: Refactor EvaluationForm and related classes to use FormGroupList and FormCriteriaList\n\n- Updated EvaluationForm to replace IImmutableList<FormGroup> with FormGroupList.\n- Updated EvaluationForm to replace IImmutableList<FormCriterion> with FormCriteriaList.\n- Modified IEvaluationForm interface to reflect changes in Groups and Criteria return types.\n- Refactored WeightedMeanPolicy and WeightedMeanPolicyDefinition to accommodate new list types.\n- Adjusted RunFormSnapshot and RunCriterionScore to utilize new FormGroupList and FormCriteriaList.\n- Created FormGroupList and FormCriteriaList value objects to encapsulate collections of FormGroup and FormCriterion respectively.\n- Updated unit te