q","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FredoqCorp/module-evaluations/commits/7a4b9cb86e2bc4f134bf19195bbc1f790e6ffce1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-18T10:46:18Z","email":"Fredoq@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Fredoq"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-18T10:46:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Refactor (#5)\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor: update FormDesign and FormGroup to use FormCriterion for criteria representation\n\n* refactor: update comments for clarity in FormDesign and FormGroup, and add EvaluationForms DbSet in DatabaseContext\n\n* Add initial evaluation form schema and migration scripts\n\n- Created DatabaseContextModelSnapshot for Entity Framework migrations.\n- Added SQL migration script to create the initial evaluation form schema, including tables for criteria, forms, form runs, form groups, form criteria, criterion automation, criterion options, and run criteria.\n- Implemented checks to ensure schema and tables are created only if they do not already exist.\n- Established foreign key relationships and unique constraints for data integrity.\n\n* refactor: remove unused EvaluationFormRepositoryQueries class\n\n* refactor: update GetAsync method to use AsSplitQuery for improved performance\n\n* refactor: remove EvaluationFormConfiguration class and its configuration methods\n\n* Add EF Core configuration for evaluation forms (#4)\n\n* Remove obsolete migration files and model snapshot for the evaluation forms schema, cleaning up the codebase and ensuring no unused artifacts remain.\n\n* ref\n\n* feat: add formcriterion configuration\n\n* feat: add evaluationform configuration\n\n* feat: add other configurations\n\n* fixes\n\n* Add initial database migration for evaluations module\n\n- Created the initial migration for the evaluations module, establishing the database schema with the necessary tables and relationships.\n- Defined tables for criteria, evaluation forms, form runs, criterion automation, criterion options, form groups, and run criteria.\n- Implemented various constraints and indexes to ensure data integrity and optimize query performance.\n- Configured PostgreSQL enums for form calculation kinds, form statuses, and optimization goals.\n\n* Add initial database migration for evaluations module\n\n- Created schema ''evaluations'' and defined necessary tables including criteria, evaluation_forms, form_runs, criterion_automation, criterion_options, form_groups, run_criteria, and form_criteria.\n- Implemented enum types for form_calculation_kind, form_status, and optimization_goal.\n- Added constraints and indexes to ensure data integrity and optimize query performance.\n- Generated corresponding SQL script for the migration.\n\n* feat: indexes\n\n* feat: refactor Weight value object and add BpsOfPercent value object\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: r.osipin <r.osipin@whyhappen.ru>","tree":{"sha":"1b3ad7a418e0f94e2da9634c33304924c77a9015","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FredoqCorp/module-evaluations/git/trees/1b3ad7a418e0f94e2da9634c33304924c77a9015"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FredoqCorp/module-evaluations/git/commits/7a4b9cb86e2bc4f134bf19195bbc1f790e6ffce1","verification":{"payload":"tree 1b3ad7a418e0f94e2da9634c33304924c77a9015\nparent 3f6de6276cec4646d995aec0128a610230ac6f6f\nauthor Fredoq <Fredoq@users.noreply.github.com> 1755513978 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1755513978 +0300\n\nRefactor (#5)\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor\n\n* refactor: update FormDesign and FormGroup to use FormCriterion for criteria representation\n\n* refactor: update comments for clarity in FormDesign and FormGroup, and add EvaluationForms DbSet in DatabaseContext\n\n* Add initial evaluation form schema and migration scripts\n\n- Created DatabaseContextModelSnapshot for Entity Framework migrations.\n- Added SQL migration script to create the initial evaluation form schema, including tables for criteria, forms, form runs, form groups, form criteria, criterion automation, criterion options, and run criteria.\n- Implemented checks to ensure schema and tables are created only if they do not already exist.\n- Established foreign key relationships and unique constraints for data integrity.\n\n* refactor: remove unused EvaluationFormRepositoryQueries class\n\n* refactor: update GetAsync method to use AsSplitQuery for improved performance\n\n* refactor: remove EvaluationFormConfiguration class and its configuration methods\n\n* Add EF Core configuration for evaluation forms (#4)\n\n* Remove obsolete migration files and model snapshot for the evaluation forms schema, cleaning up the codebase and ensuring no unused artifacts remain.\n\n* ref\n\n* feat: add formcriterion configuration\n\n* feat: add evaluationform configuration\n\n* feat: add other configurations\n\n* fixes\n\n* Add initial database migration for evaluations module\n\n- Created the initial migration for the evaluations module, establishing the database schema with the necessary tables and relationships.\n- Defined tables for criteria, evaluation forms, form runs, criterion automation, criterion options, form groups, and run criteria.\n- Implemented various constraints and indexes to ensure data integrity and optimize query performance.\n- Configured PostgreSQL enums for form calculation kinds, form statuses, and optimization goals.\n\n* Add initial database migration for evaluations module\n\n- Created schema ''evaluations'' and defined necessary tables including criteria, evaluation_forms, form_runs, criterion_automation, criterion_options, form_groups, run_criteria, and form_criteria.\n- Implemented enum types for form_calculation_kind, form_status, and optimization_goal.\n- Added constraints and indexes to ensure data integrity and optimize query performance.\n- Generated corresponding SQL script for the migration.\n\n* feat: indexes\n\n* feat: refactor Weight value object and add BpsOfPercent value object\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: r.osipin <r.osipin@whyhappen.ru>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoowR6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/t8QAGcNuNgoJu3+/WWnMETWNS27\nRy6/yTld6a1jH1ZQKqw70MP+dPglMcd87SK7iw2Tn4R9h+rk1rDAZwxHOMSTpMV1\nXKIOKShLZQyrY5YHLBLj92vkgiTf2mNrDfoGqlKfg1s5XnlY7kllzkfpcZhZNZ/8\nifFBXR7h5uCkk26VsOoC90PgbBRnTZspqfXsnT7h2J4yvemD8Tk/iWuEZcgkJW9T\n4ibXUR9rr75U+8SQbyDW4rchuLJ+jHuXvA1brm1cybAhH1qc+mjnUdoyHRRgsIkO\nPbdfCl6OwUnRNU95Q2Nlm+CklulfW8FutJdgsNxi9YZVJKuRyNBdxQ9LansHLIBH\nI354OAKVhkJobgWiREUvY0fwe7mod6zGtZfxSN04aSFC/C2SgCY5lnbDZfigfMhB\nhyVZJlKfQ/U9awRstM2pDzVlw8ZWb4NhPPD9a1/FOMThqkiUmMRswxz7E8N8zVAM\nqRMveoMienYAIqcVxSA3V9XNU0Ds0usUpkQM7mX4euva3wEw43Gn9lQ5QCHi/i5H\nMQsNa3Vy7z4ZbXV3WELEMY+e41tYLHQR54Nl7I8a/gjiVAGZZiHdzjVeGo+7y9gZ\njhEiEH48wNQPDrZDYaH56/fRNjWDIvdD96VyDdamzy+NhrbiSUWBr7hCtmE0/LWG\nZKMt5XRnhgslSJK53pEJ\n=JoPr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-08-18T10:46:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscription