in-single-spa/pull/337\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#337</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/ir31k0\"><code>@​ir31k0</code></a> made\ntheir first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/337\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#337</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/compare/v1.0.0...v1.1.0\">https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/compare/v1.0.0...v1.1.0</a></p>\n<h2>v1.0.0</h2>\n<p>Welcome to the first stable release! After 1 year, 8 months and 14\ndays since the first experimental version, we have reached full semantic\nversioning support.</p>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump mocha from 10.8.2 to 11.0.1 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/258\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#258</a></li>\n<li>build: Add bash script by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/gsingh-ds\"><code>@​gsingh-ds</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/278\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#278</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump ts-mocha from 10.0.0 to 11.1.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/291\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#291</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump <code>@​types/node</code> from 22.10.5 to\n22.13.4 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/288\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#288</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump publint from 0.3.0 to 0.3.6 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/290\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#290</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump chai from 5.1.2 to 5.2.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/289\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#289</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump mocha from 10.8.2 to 11.1.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/279\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#279</a></li>\n<li>chore: Upgrade non-major of packages by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/webJose\"><code>@​webJose</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/293\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#293</a></li>\n<li>build(deps): Bump esbuild and vite by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/294\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#294</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/gsingh-ds\"><code>@​gsingh-ds</code></a>\nmade their first contribution in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/278\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#278</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/compare/v0.9.0...v1.0.0\">https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/compare/v0.9.0...v1.0.0</a></p>\n<h2>v0.9.0</h2>\n<p>This version adds no new functionality. It is the first generation of\nthe repository after being simplified (to just one package.json file).\nIt contains one potentially breaking change: The <code>resolveId</code>\nhook''s order is now <code>pre</code> to finally get rid of one error\nthat publint kept complaining about.</p>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>feat: Reorganize package contents by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/webJose\"><code>@​webJose</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/256\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#256</a></li>\n<li>fix: Remove ex/index.ts to avoid rollup being confused by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/webJose\"><code>@​webJose</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/264\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#264</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump vite from 6.0.1 to 6.0.5 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/263\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#263</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump <code>@​types/node</code> from 22.10.0 to\n22.10.5 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/266\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#266</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump typescript from 5.7.2 to 5.7.3 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/270\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#270</a></li>\n<li>build(deps-dev): Bump publint from 0.2.12 to 0.3.0 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/268\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#268</a></li>\n<li>build(deps): Bump vite from 6.0.1 to 6.0.7 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/dependabot\"><code>@​dependabot</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/271\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#271</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/compare/v0.8.1...v0.9.0\">https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/compare/v0.8.1...v0.9.0</a></p>\n<h2>v0.8.1</h2>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<h3>Plug-In</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>fix: Allow higher versions of Vite v6 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/webJose\"><code>@​webJose</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/pull/254\">WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa#254</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/c0c7bce46313f7800b151b3d080732ea341e2888\"><code>c0c7bce</code></a>\n1.1.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/c6e177960664a2d6f1db7d22f752e4bbcc87b799\"><code>c6e1779</code></a>\nfix: Allow Vite version ^7.0.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/337\">#337</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/29fec87b8a7e2a4287cdee263b38c39b35f0d63a\"><code>29fec87</code></a>\ndocs: Update README (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/315\">#315</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/716399a8713d1f1d6ef0966891beedd0c3bb2149\"><code>716399a</code></a>\n1.0.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/5d603ff7a22818b11f2bc7a5595d403e5c8cb82d\"><code>5d603ff</code></a>\nbuild(deps): Bump esbuild and vite (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/294\">#294</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/52ad2be5a21dfa8e941c73c9dcb70e234390135e\"><code>52ad2be</code></a>\nchore: Upgrade non-major of packages (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/293\">#293</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/40090fbc7ae8b3563a571fa73ceb523d6de1ea9d\"><code>40090fb</code></a>\nbuild(deps-dev): Bump mocha from 10.8.2 to 11.1.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/279\">#279</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/ce812a9f9c04c60eacfb8a7ba9bfc655023203c9\"><code>ce812a9</code></a>\nbuild(deps-dev): Bump chai from 5.1.2 to 5.2.0 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/289\">#289</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/9fd0562b741bbe0984154271faba845948757acd\"><code>9fd0562</code></a>\nbuild(deps-dev): Bump publint from 0.3.0 to 0.3.6 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/290\">#290</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/commit/e06df1bbe3ee56901f8c95c63120485d103fc1b8\"><code>e06df1b</code></a>\nbuild(deps-dev): Bump <code>@​types/node</code> from 22.10.5 to 22.13.4\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/issues/288\">#288</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa/compare/v0.7.0...v1.1.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot merge` will merge this PR after your CI passes on it\n- `@dependabot squash and merge` will squash and merge this PR after\nyour CI passes on it\n- `@dependabot cancel merge` will cancel a previously requested merge\nand block automerging\n- `@dependabot reopen` will reopen this PR if it is closed\n- `@dependabot close` will close this PR and stop Dependabot recreating\nit. You can achieve the same result by closing it manually\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/Agile-Software-Engineering-25/root-ui/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e14ab1601c6ff4a908efacb8cdeb2220b9d5b3db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agile-Software-Engineering-25/root-ui/git/trees/e14ab1601c6ff4a908efacb8cdeb2220b9d5b3db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agile-Software-Engineering-25/root-ui/git/commits/8caed7ca29bcf8d22bb7ead82cdf11768e7ca274","verification":{"payload":"tree e14ab1601c6ff4a908efacb8cdeb2220b9d5b3db\nparent 2e6336de05d3714c66051adcc5038429847ae0eb\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1759228773 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1759228773 +0200\n\nBump esbuild, vite and vite-plugin-single-spa (#12)\n\nBumps [esbuild](https://github.com/evanw/esbuild) to 0.25.10 and updates\nancestor dependencies [esbuild](https://github.com/evanw/esbuild),\n[vite](https://github.com/vitejs/vite/tree/HEAD/packages/vite) and\n[vite-plugin-single-spa](https://github.com/WJSoftware/vite-plugin-single-spa).\nThese dependencies need to be updated together.\n\nUpdates `esbuild` from 0.21.5 to 0.25.10\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/releases\">esbuild''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v0.25.10</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix a panic in a minification edge case (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4287\">#4287</a>)</p>\n<p>This release fixes a panic due to a null pointer that could happen\nwhen esbuild inlines a doubly-nested identity function and the final\nresult is empty. It was fixed by emitting the value\n<code>undefined</code> in this case, which avoids the panic. This case\nmust be rare since it hasn''t come up until now. Here is an example of\ncode that previously triggered the panic (which only happened when\nminifying):</p>\n<pre lang=\"js\"><code>function identity(x) { return x }\nidentity({ y: identity(123) })\n</code></pre>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Fix <code>@supports</code> nested inside pseudo-element (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4265\">#4265</a>)</p>\n<p>When transforming nested CSS to non-nested CSS, esbuild is supposed\nto filter out pseudo-elements such as <code>::placeholder</code> for\ncorrectness. The <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/css-nesting-1/\">CSS\nnesting specification</a> says the following:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The nesting selector cannot represent pseudo-elements (identical to\nthe behavior of the '':is()'' pseudo-class). We’d like to relax this\nrestriction, but need to do so simultaneously for both '':is()'' and\n''&amp;'', since they’re intentionally built on the same underlying\nmechanisms.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>However, it seems like this behavior is different for nested at-rules\nsuch as <code>@supports</code>, which do work with pseudo-elements. So\nthis release modifies esbuild''s behavior to now take that into\naccount:</p>\n<pre lang=\"css\"><code>/* Original code */\n::placeholder {\n  color: red;\n  body &amp; { color: green }\n  @supports (color: blue) { color: blue }\n}\n<p>/* Old output (with --supported:nesting=false) */<br />\n::placeholder {<br />\ncolor: red;<br />\n}<br />\nbody :is() {<br />\ncolor: green;<br />\n}<br />\n<a href=\"https://github.com/supports\"><code>@​supports</code></a>\n(color: blue) {<br />\n{<br />\ncolor: blue;<br />\n}<br />\n}</p>\n<p>/* New output (with --supported:nesting=false) */<br />\n::placeholder {<br />\ncolor: red;<br />\n}<br />\nbody :is() {<br />\ncolor: green;<br />\n}<br />\n<a href=\"https://github.com/supports\"><code>@​supports</code></a>\n(color: blue) {<br />\n::placeholder {<br />\ncolor: blue;<br />\n}<br />\n</code></pre></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/blob/main/CHANGELOG-2024.md\">esbuild''s\nchangelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>Changelog: 2024</h1>\n<p>This changelog documents all esbuild versions published in the year\n2024 (versions 0.19.12 through 0.24.2).</p>\n<h2>0.24.2</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Fix regression with <code>--define</code> and\n<code>import.meta</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4010\">#4010</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4012\">#4012</a>,\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/pull/4013\">#4013</a>)</p>\n<p>The previous change in version 0.24.1 to use a more expression-like\nparser for <code>define</code> values to allow quoted property names\nintroduced a regression that removed the ability to use\n<code>--define:import.meta=...</code>. Even though <code>import</code>\nis normally a keyword that can''t be used as an identifier, ES modules\nspecial-case the <code>import.meta</code> expression to behave like an\nidentifier anyway. This change fixes the regression.</p>\n<p>This fix was contributed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/sapphi-red\"><code>@​sapphi-red</code></a>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>0.24.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Allow <code>es2024</code> as a target in <code>tsconfig.json</code>\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4004\">#4004</a>)</p>\n<p>TypeScript recently <a\nhref=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-5-7/#support-for---target-es2024-and---lib-es2024\">added\n<code>es2024</code></a> as a compilation target, so esbuild now supports\nthis in the <code>target</code> field of <code>tsconfig.json</code>\nfiles, such as in the following configuration file:</p>\n<pre lang=\"json\"><code>{\n  &quot;compilerOptions&quot;: {\n    &quot;target&quot;: &quot;ES2024&quot;\n  }\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>As a reminder, the only thing that esbuild uses this field for is\ndetermining whether or not to use legacy TypeScript behavior for class\nfields. You can read more in <a\nhref=\"https://esbuild.github.io/content-types/#tsconfig-json\">the\ndocumentation</a>.</p>\n<p>This fix was contributed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/billyjanitsch\"><code>@​billyjanitsch</code></a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Allow automatic semicolon insertion after\n<code>get</code>/<code>set</code></p>\n<p>This change fixes a grammar bug in the parser that incorrectly\ntreated the following code as a syntax error:</p>\n<pre lang=\"ts\"><code>class Foo {\n  get\n  *x() {}\n  set\n  *y() {}\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>The above code will be considered valid starting with this release.\nThis change to esbuild follows a <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/pull/60225\">similar\nchange to TypeScript</a> which will allow this syntax starting with\nTypeScript 5.7.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Allow quoted property names in <code>--define</code> and\n<code>--pure</code> (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4008\">#4008</a>)</p>\n<p>The <code>define</code> and <code>pure</code> API options now accept\nidentifier expressions containing quoted property names. Previously all\nidentifiers in the identifier expression had to be bare identifiers.\nThis change now makes <code>--define</code> and <code>--pure</code>\nconsistent with <code>--global-name</code>, which already supported\nquoted property names. For example, the following is now possible:</p>\n<pre lang=\"js\"><code></code></pre>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/d6b668f96fb00d6a6d035f058e38b6bd2507beb6\"><code>d6b668f</code></a>\npublish 0.25.10 to npm</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/5088c198b5ecee18ba903c4099458df98b1b6788\"><code>5088c19</code></a>\nrefactor: use strings.Builder (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4290\">#4290</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/755da31752d759f1ea70b8d4f7f677b3557dab3e\"><code>755da31</code></a>\nrun <code>make update-compat-table</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/a1d9c8649bcbacc59e521171f47d6928fda14043\"><code>a1d9c86</code></a>\nfix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4287\">#4287</a>:\nmarked the wrong issue as fixed</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/73a0b2ae491c9d6a069516447292df2afe371b63\"><code>73a0b2a</code></a>\nfix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4286\">#4286</a>:\nminifier panic due to identity function</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/134dadffecf55c5dba20cd9f03996275da06ba49\"><code>134dadf</code></a>\nfix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/4265\">#4265</a>:\n<code>@supports</code> nested inside <code>::pseudo</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/195e05c16f03a341390feef38b8ebf17d3075e14\"><code>195e05c</code></a>\npublish 0.25.9 to npm</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/3dac33f2a2ba60387fb9aaca96b3e80b9e0512e0\"><code>3dac33f</code></a>\nfix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/3131\">#3131</a>,\nfix <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/evanw/esbuild/issues/3663\">#3663</a>:\nyarnpnp + windows + D drive</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/0f2c5c8c11dc3fa2a4e9e82df202d0b607e59de4\"><code>0f2c5c8</code></a>\nmock fs now supports multiple volumes on windows</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/commit/100a51e791ce714a1a90557bc9e5133fa0d38692\"><code>100a51e</code></a>\nsplit out yarnpnp snapshot tests</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/evanw/esbuild/compare/v0.21.5...v0.25.10\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `vite` from 5.4.19 to 7.1.7\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/releases\">vite''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v7.1.7</h2>\n<p>Please refer to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/v7.1.7/packages/vite/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>\nfor details.</p>\n<h2>v7.1.6</h2>\n<p>Please refer to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/v7.1.6/packages/vite/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>\nfor details.</p>\n<h2>v7.1.5</h2>\n<p>Please refer to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/v7.1.5/packages/vite/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>\nfor details.</p>\n<h2>v7.1.4</h2>\n<p>Please refer to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/v7.1.4/packages/vite/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>\nfor details.</p>\n<h2>v7.1.3</h2>\n<p>Please refer to <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/v7.1.3/packages/vite/CHANGELOG.md\">CHANGELOG.md</a>\nfor details.</p>\n<h2>create-vite